1️⃣ What is Multithreading?
✅ Definition:

Multithreading means running multiple threads concurrently within a single process to perform tasks in parallel.

Each thread is a lightweight sub-process.

Threads share the same memory but run independently.

💡 Example:
class MyThread extends Thread {
    public void run() {
        System.out.println("Thread running: " + Thread.currentThread().getName());
    }
}

public class ThreadExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        MyThread t1 = new MyThread();
        MyThread t2 = new MyThread();

        t1.start();   // start new thread
        t2.start();
    }
}


Output:

Thread running: Thread-0
Thread running: Thread-1

